Verdict: ❌ Does not meet pequirements

Pages & Structure: All required pages exist, Folder structure partially follows requirements.

Visual Accuracy: Layout is close but not pixel-perfect; spacing, typography, and proportions are approximated. Heavy reliance on fixed sizes.

HTML Quality: Overuse of <div>s, weak semantic structure, inline scripts repeated across pages.

CSS Quality: Large monolithic CSS file, duplicated rules, inconsistent spacing, and visible errors (line-height: 1.5;in). Not clean or maintainable.

Responsiveness: Hamburger menu works, but mobile layout hacks (height: 158vh, !important) indicate poor responsiveness strategy.

Functionality: Some interactivity (menu toggle, slider, settings storage) exists, but search is dummy and JS is inline instead of modular.

Accessibility: Very limited. Missing labels, focus states, ARIA roles, and keyboard handling.

Best Practices & SEO: Basic meta tags only. No keywords, lazy loading, consistent integrity usage, or README.


Remark: Submission by Abdul Wahab shows stronger effort than basic static layouts, including navigation and sliders, but fails pixel-perfect accuracy, code cleanliness, accessibility, best practices, and production-ready standards.